@startuml secure-login-flow
' Sample PUML for parser tests — hardened against the STRIDE findings from the backend.
title Sample Login Flow (STRIDE-Hardened)
skinparam shadowing false

actor "End User" as user
participant "CDN + WAF" as waf
participant "Web App" as web
boundary "Auth Gateway" as authgw
control     "Auth Service"   as auth
entity      "Secret Manager" as vault
participant "DB Firewall"    as dbfw
database    "User DB"        as udb
queue       "Audit Queue"    as q
participant "SIEM"           as siem

user   -->  waf    : HTTPS request
waf    -->  web    : forward over TLS
web    -->  web    : input validation
web    --> authgw : credentials (mTLS)
authgw ->  auth   : validate
auth   ->  vault  : fetch signing keys
auth   ->  dbfw   : query user
dbfw   -->  udb    : authorized SELECT
udb    --> dbfw   : profile
dbfw   --> auth   : profile
auth   --> q      : signed audit event
q      --> siem   : ship logs
auth   --> web    : generic reject on invalid

note right of waf
  Mitigates Web D and T:
  rate-limit, WAF rules (OWASP CRS),
  bot and scraping filters.
end note

note right of web
  Mitigates Web S, T, I, R, E:
  TLS 1.2+ with HSTS,
  CSP and Subresource Integrity,
  custom error pages and no debug in prod,
  centralized auth logs,
  OWASP secure coding, SAST and DAST in CI.
end note

note right of authgw
  Mitigates S:
  mTLS between Web App and Auth,
  rejects non-mTLS clients.
end note

note right of auth
  Mitigates E and R:
  MFA required for admin actions,
  least privilege,
  tamper-evident auth logs,
  account lockout and adaptive throttling.
end note

note right of dbfw
  Mitigates DB I and E:
  DB firewall blocks anomalous queries,
  IDS alerts forwarded to SIEM.
end note

note right of udb
  Mitigates DB T, I, D, E:
  Transparent Data Encryption at rest,
  TLS in transit from app tier,
  least-privilege DB user (no DDL),
  connection pooling and query timeout,
  read replicas for resilience,
  MFA for human admin access.
end note

note right of q
  Mitigates R:
  append-only signed audit events,
  forwarded to SIEM for retention,
  tamper-evident hash chain.
end note

@enduml
